WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

This license applies to the *derived layer* authored here: the summaries,
cross-talk syntheses, concept definitions, maturity labels, speaker pages,
corpus structure, and the selection and arrangement of the material.

It does NOT apply to the underlying talks. This wiki quotes Y Combinator
Startup School 2026 speakers in excerpt, with attribution and a deep link to the
source video at the exact timestamp on Y Combinator's own YouTube channel.
Copyright in those talks, and in the quoted words themselves, belongs to the
speakers and to Y Combinator. Nothing here grants you rights to that material,
and the CC BY grant above cannot and does not extend to it.

This repository deliberately ships no full transcripts. Excerpts plus deep links
are intended to send readers to the original talks rather than substitute for
them.

If you are a speaker or an event organizer and want a quote, a page, or an
attribution corrected or removed, please open an issue on the repository.

Code in this event directory is licensed separately under the MIT License. See
the `LICENSE` file one level up.
